025\",\"cover\":\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/holographic-utopia-after-80-cover.webp\",\"roles\":[\"Music Design\"]}</script>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\n\n\t\t\t<section class=\"work-detail__section work-detail__section--description\" data-work-detail-section=\"ABOUT\" aria-labelledby=\"work-detail-section-description-113\"><h2 class=\"work-detail__label\" id=\"work-detail-section-description-113\"><span class=\"work-detail__label-text\">ABOUT</span></h2><div class=\"work-detail__section-body\"><div class=\"work-detail__post-content work-detail__description\"><h2 class=\"wp-block-heading screen-reader-text\">Description</h2>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a future where technology can shape anything at will, do the happiness and freedom that humanity truly seeks</p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">really exist in that flawless holographic utopia?</p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Built around holographic interactive projection technology, the Holographic Utopia exhibition speculates on a worldview in which the virtual and the real interweave and the boundary between imagination and reality blurs. The exhibition invites visitors into an ideal realm that they can freely construct and project themselves into, imagining how technology becomes a tangible tool for contemporary society's pursuit of “utopia”. Here, visitors can switch identities, environments and situations in real time and rethink what a “perfect world” means.</p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The exhibition grew out of “A Future Society of Sustainable Empathy: A Sensory Revolution of Holographic Interaction”, a sub-project of the National Science and Technology Council (NSTC) Humanities × Integrated Circuits Program. The series includes After the Age of 80 and The Paul Trio; through a series of workshops, four outstanding hybrid, cross-disciplinary proposals were also selected — Developing Solution, Future Sensory Experience Trading, Bai Zu Yun and PM 3000 — to imagine utopia together.</p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The exhibition also raises questions about future ways of living, social structures and ethics, prompting visitors to reflect: when the beauty of a virtual world can be created and modified at will, will the imperfections and genuine emotions of real life be overlooked? In a fully digitised future, will our relationships with the environment, with others and even with ourselves be reshaped into some “idealised” illusion? The exhibition also touches on power and the distribution of resources. Who has the power to create holographic worlds? Who decides the rules of these virtual utopias? When technology becomes a tool for controlling reality, will the holographic utopia reflect yet another metaphor of class and control?</p>\n</div></div></section>\n\t\t\t<section class=\"work-detail__section work-detail__section--listen\" data-work-detail-section=\"LISTEN\" aria-labelledby=\"work-detail-section-listen-113\"><h2 class=\"work-detail__label\" id=\"work-detail-section-listen-113\"><span class=\"work-detail__label-text\">LISTEN</span></h2><div class=\"work-detail__section-body\"><div class=\"work-media work-media--listen\"><div class=\"work-media__block work-media__block--tracks\"><p class=\"work-media__heading\" aria-hidden=\"true\">Tracks</p><section class=\"work-media__section work-detail-audio\" data-work-detail-audio data-playlist-work-id=\"113\" data-playlist-title=\"Holographic Utopia: After the Age of 80\" aria-labelledby=\"work-detail-audio-113\"><h2 id=\"work-detail-audio-113\" class=\"work-detail-audio__title screen-reader-text\">Holographic Utopia: After the Age of 80</h2><ol class=\"work-detail-audio__tracks\"><li class=\"work-detail-audio__track-item\">Holographic Utopia After the Age of 80 score ExhVer</li><li class=\"work-detail-audio__track-item\">Holographic Utopia After the Age of 80 score</li></ol><script type=\"application/json\" data-work-detail-audio-tracks>[{\"id\":115,\"attachment_id\":115,\"work_id\":113,\"title\"